(Northwind Components Ltd. - Sustainable Supply Chain & ESG Policy \(FY2025\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This is a fictional sample policy created for the Supply Chain AI Copilot demo. Replace it with) Tj T*
(real sustainability reports \(for example annual ESG reports published by large electronics) Tj T*
(manufacturers\) for a realistic evaluation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Section 1. Purpose and Scope) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1.1 This policy defines environmental, social and governance \(ESG\) requirements for all inbound) Tj T*
(and outbound logistics, contract manufacturers and tier-1 suppliers of Northwind Components.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1.2 The policy applies to all product lines, including SKU-101 \(USB-C docking station\), SKU-102) Tj T*
(\(27-inch monitor\), SKU-103 \(wireless keyboard\), SKU-104 \(laptop battery pack\) and SKU-105) Tj T*
(\(recycled-aluminium laptop stand\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Section 2. Climate Targets) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2.1 Northwind commits to reduce absolute Scope 1 and Scope 2 greenhouse gas emissions by 50) Tj T*
(percent by 2030 against a 2020 baseline, and to reach net-zero emissions across the value chain) Tj T*
(by 2045.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2.2 Scope 3 upstream transportation and distribution emissions must fall by 30 percent per unit) Tj T*
(shipped by 2030. Logistics emissions are calculated as distance in kilometres multiplied by) Tj T*
(shipment weight in tonnes multiplied by the transport-mode emission factor, consistent with the) Tj T*
(GLEC Framework.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2.3 Default emission factors in kilograms of CO2e per tonne-kilometre are: road truck 0.105,) Tj T*
(rail 0.028, ocean freight 0.016 and air freight 0.500.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Section 3. Transport Mode Rules) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3.1 Air freight may only be used for shipments that are critical to production continuity or) Tj T*
(customer safety, and requires written approval from the Regional Logistics Director.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3.2 Shipments over 500 kilometres within continental Europe or North America should use rail or) Tj T*
(intermodal transport when the delivery window allows at least five business days.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3.3 SKU-104 laptop battery packs contain lithium-ion cells and are classified as dangerous) Tj T*
(goods \(UN3480\). They must never be shipped as passenger-aircraft cargo and must follow IATA) Tj T*
(packing instruction 965 when air freight is approved.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Section 4. Supplier Requirements) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4.1 Tier-1 suppliers must report their energy use and Scope 1 and 2 emissions annually through) Tj T*
(the CDP supply chain programme.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4.2 By 2027, 80 percent of procurement spend must be with suppliers that have set science-based) Tj T*
(emission reduction targets validated by the SBTi.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4.3 Suppliers must source at least 50 percent renewable electricity by 2028 and 100 percent by) Tj T*
ET
